# Talish Talks - Netlify redirects
#
# The frontend is a single-page application: the router owns every path, so
# a direct request for a client-side route must be answered with the
# application shell instead of a 404.
#
# Only the application's own routes are listed here. `/api/*` and
# `/socket.io/*` are deliberately left out so the proxy rules that forward
# live traffic to the backend keep working - a blanket `/*` rule would
# shadow them and break authentication and messaging.
#
# The file lives in `frontend/public`, so Vite copies it into `frontend/dist`
# and Netlify picks it up from the publish directory.

/signin     /index.html  200
/register   /index.html  200
/chat/*     /index.html  200
/contacts   /index.html  200
/profile    /index.html  200
/settings   /index.html  200
/404        /index.html  200
